🔍 Splunk SIEM Log Analysis Projects
A hands-on collection of 7 cybersecurity projects focused on analyzing different types of network logs using Splunk SIEM. Each project covers uploading log data, writing SPL queries, detecting anomalies, and monitoring traffic patterns.

🛠️ Tools Used

Splunk SIEM
SPL (Splunk Processing Language)
Zeek IDS (for Tunnel logs)
Sample log datasets from secrepo.com


📁 Projects
#ProjectProtocolWhat I Analyzed1DNS Log AnalysisDNSQuery patterns, suspicious domains, anomalies2FTP Log AnalysisFTPFile transfer activity, failed logins, anomalies3HTTP Log AnalysisHTTPRequest patterns, error codes, suspicious traffic4SSH Log AnalysisSSHBrute force attempts, login activity, correlations5Tunnel Log AnalysisGRE/IPv4/IPv6Tunnel traffic detection, threat correlation6SMTP Log AnalysisSMTPEmail traffic patterns, spam detection, anomalies7DHCP Log AnalysisDHCPIP assignments, rogue devices, anomalies

🎯 Skills Demonstrated

Uploading and indexing log data into Splunk
Writing SPL queries for search, filtering, and statistics
Extracting relevant fields from raw log data
Detecting anomalies and suspicious behavior
Correlating logs across multiple data sources


